    "title": "Debugging Tip: Always Check the Basics 🛠️",
    "content": "When troubleshooting a bug, start by verifying the basics: input validation, edge cases, and environment setup. Often, the solution lies in something simple rather than a complex logic error. 🧠💡

**Example:**
```js
// ❌ Bad practice
if (userInput) {
  // do something
}
```

**✅ Better approach:**
```js
// Check for falsy values explicitly
if (userInput && typeof userInput === 'string') {
  // do something
}
```

Remember: A well-structured test case can save hours of frustration. 🧪"
}

